            "keyPoints": [
                "5.79 billion social identities — about 7 in 10 people on Earth — as of April 2026.",
                "The average person uses 6.75 platforms a month, so single-platform posting reaches a fraction of the audience.",
                "Over 1 million YouTube channels used the platform's own AI creation tools every day in December 2025.",
                "Meta says same-day posts now make up over 30% of recommended Reels — posting speed is distribution.",
                "49% of marketers rank short-form video as their highest-ROI content format in 2026.",
                "Goldman Sachs projects the creator economy addressable market near $480B by 2027, from ~$250B.",
                "Only ~4% of the world's ~50 million creators earn over $100,000 a year — output and consistency separate them.",
                "YouTube's CEO frames AI as 'a tool for expression, not a replacement' while making 'AI slop' a 2026 enforcement priority — volume alone is no longer a moat."
